INT. FERRIS WHEEL GONDOLA 14 - COMPLAINTS DEPARTMENT - DAY

A decommissioned gondola bolted to a service platform. Two desks. One window. One fire extinguisher nobody trusts.

PRIYA RAMANATHAN, thirties, headset, ironed blouse. Armour.

HUGH BELLAMY, fifties, comb-over, mug reading WORLD'S OKAYEST BOSS. He leans in the doorway.

HUGH
Priya. Quarterly numbers.

PRIYA
Good.

HUGH
Good?

PRIYA
Complaints are down forty percent.

HUGH
Brilliant.

PRIYA
Because the phone line's been unplugged since June.

Hugh freezes. Smile stuck.

HUGH
Unplugged.

PRIYA
By you. For "restructuring."

Hugh enters. Sits on the desk. Sighs like a man in a hot-air balloon.

HUGH
Okay. Okay. Nobody tells Corporate.

PRIYA
Corporate's in the next gondola.

CORDELL "CORKY" WASHINGTON, twenties, pops up from under the other desk. Headphones. Cheese puff dust on his lip.

CORKY
Morning!

HUGH
You live here?

CORKY
Gondola's got Wi-Fi.

The gondola sways. All three grab something.

PRIYA
Why are we moving?

CORKY
Wheel's on. Maintenance said "test."

HUGH
Test what?

CORKY
Whether it still goes.

The gondola lifts. Rises. Through the window the city tilts into view. Hugh's mug slides. He catches it.

An old PHONE on the wall RINGS. Everyone stares.

PRIYA
That's connected?

HUGH
That's not supposed to be connected.

Ring. Ring. Priya answers. Puts it on speaker.

PRIYA
Complaints. Priya.

MS. FENWICK-ADEYEMI (V.O.)
(over phone, crisp)
Ms. Ramanathan. Marjorie Fenwick-Adeyemi. Head of Customer Experience.

Hugh mouths: Corporate. Corky mouths: In the next gondola.

MS. FENWICK-ADEYEMI (V.O.) (CONT'D)
I'm told your department has had no complaints in four months.

PRIYA
That's correct.

MS. FENWICK-ADEYEMI (V.O.)
It's the most impressive thing I've ever seen.

Hugh straightens. Smiles. Corky gives a thumbs-up.

MS. FENWICK-ADEYEMI (V.O.) (CONT'D)
I'd like to put you in charge of the whole company.

PRIYA
(beat)
What?

HUGH
(whisper)
Say yes.

MS. FENWICK-ADEYEMI (V.O.)
Mr. Bellamy is, of course, being let go.

Hugh's mug hits the floor.

HUGH
What?!

CORKY
Oh, wow.

PRIYA
(into phone)
Can I call you back?

MS. FENWICK-ADEYEMI (V.O.)
I'm in the next gondola.

They all turn. Through the window, ten feet away, a woman in a grey suit lifts a phone. Waves.

The wheel stops. Hangs. Wind. Silence.

Hugh drops onto the desk.

HUGH
Priya. I trained you.

PRIYA
You taught me where the mute button was.

HUGH
That's training!

CORKY
(to no one)
I can see her lunch.

Priya hangs up. Looks at Hugh. At the extinguisher. At the city below.

PRIYA
I have a condition.

HUGH
Anything.

PRIYA
Plug the phones back in.

HUGH
(horrified)
Why?

PRIYA
So we can hear what people actually think.

Hugh gulps. The wheel jolts. It starts to descend.

CORKY
That's going to be loud.

HUGH
How loud?

CORKY
(shrugs, eats a puff)
Gondola loud.

The wheel carries them down into the noise of the city.
